{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_troubleshooting", "label": "Troubleshooting catalog", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Organised by symptom rather than by subsystem: each section names the likely causes and what to check, log or measure to confirm.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_cluster_wont_form", "label": "Symptom: cluster will not form", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Check in order - unreachable seeds from wrong addresses, DNS or RBAC; a firewalled cluster port; different ActorSystem names on different nodes; a silently failing TLS handshake. Confirm whether SelfUp fires at all.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_cluster_flaps", "label": "Symptom: cluster flaps", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Members oscillate between reachable and unreachable from failure-detector thresholds too tight for the network jitter, a real partition, or GC pauses longer than the unreachable threshold.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_sharded_entities_dont_spawn", "label": "Symptom: sharded entities do not spawn", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The coordinator has not started and messages are buffered, no node matches the configured role so no shards are allocated, or extractEntityId returns undefined so routing has nothing to hash.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_rebalance_storm", "label": "Symptom: rebalance storm", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Continuous rebalances from an aggressive allocation strategy with rebalanceThreshold 1 plus frequent membership changes, or a flapping cluster where every change triggers a rebalance.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_slow_actor_start", "label": "Symptom: actor takes 30 seconds to start", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A deep journal without snapshots means recovery reads every event ever written; if P99 recovery exceeds a second, set a snapshot policy.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_wrong_state_after_recovery", "label": "Symptom: events recovered but state is wrong", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "onEvent has a side effect, uses Date.now or randomness so each replay differs, or a schema change landed without an adapter so old events have a different shape.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_unbounded_memory_growth", "label": "Symptom: memory grows unboundedly", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Most often a mailbox with a slow consumer, since mailboxes are unbounded by default; then subscriber sets that never unsubscribe on stop, DistributedData keys accumulating, and stash or ask reply-to buffers.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_http_latency_under_load", "label": "Symptom: HTTP latency high under actor load", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "An actor monopolises the event loop and starves HTTP handlers; the fix is a per-actor throughput budget on the heavy actor rather than a different dispatcher.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_shutdown_dropped_messages", "label": "Symptom: shutdown dropped my messages", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "terminate drains user actors, but not past the drain budget, not a parked or throttled mailbox, not work not yet in a mailbox such as an unfired timer tick, and never for system actors which are not quiet by design.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_dead_letter_subscription_timing", "label": "Dead letters must be subscribed before the fact", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Publishing is all that happens by default, so nothing keeps a dead letter and there is nothing to read afterwards; set dead-letters.store to persistent to have the record without knowing in advance you will want it.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_flaky_timing_tests", "label": "Symptom: flaky timing-sensitive tests", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Usually a fixed sleep long enough on an idle machine and too short on a loaded runner; control time with ManualScheduler or wait on observable state. Other causes exist, and guessing between them wastes an afternoon.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_troubleshooting", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_cluster_wont_form", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_troubleshooting", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_cluster_flaps", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_troubleshooting", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_sharded_entities_dont_spawn", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_troubleshooting", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_rebalance_storm", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/troubleshooting.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_troubleshooting", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_troubleshooting_slow_actor_start", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACT